From a21b92cffd4d8d20f702b57b9463134199aa3345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:13:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sync): exclude DarkWake from outbox awake budget [daveey]

Problem: MacBook lid-closed DarkWakes advanced monotonic stale budgets despite
no full Wake (t_823c0a5431d5993d; real 2026-11-14 pmset evidence).
Why: the outbox gate added by PR3255 observes sendable identities but still
counts every monotonic interval. DarkWake runs the clock without giving sync
normal awake opportunity. Sleep tests froze that clock, missing this case.
Recurrence: same class as cron restart reruns and replica-age PR3291.

Reuse the existing cron host_fully_awake implementation through replica-age's
shared fail-awake sampler. Both outbox entrypoints sample once and suppress
alarms/exclude elapsed observation intervals when false; the dispatcher
passes the same sample to replica-age. Persist excluded seconds alongside
seen_at (already the previous observation). Legacy records default to zero.
Warned timestamps remain absolute even when exclusion moves since past them.

Accepted limits match cron/replica: an idle lid-closed Mac on AC with external
display and an idle lid-open Mac on battery read not fully awake; active use
resumes counting. Non-Mac and probe failure read awake. No wake_clock changes.

Proof: RED on unchanged outbox: both warning and card fire at 600 DarkWake s.
GREEN: 25 DarkWake minutes then ten awake minutes, mixed awake/DarkWake with
same-boot restart, warned-incident restart, legacy and invalid memo records,
probe failure, single shared dispatcher sample and alternating entrypoints.
Focused suites: 171 passed (outbox awake/observation, starvation, replica, cron).
scripts/check: all 20 checks pass. Live prevention not yet observed; owner
card retains both-detector installation, telemetry and Mac replay acceptance.
